#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""
prepper-build — build Honey Badgers from a laptop without ever storing
the OS image or the content on the laptop.

  plan    show what a tier holds, whether it fits a drive, how long it takes
  flash   stream Raspberry Pi OS straight onto the Badger's NVMe/SD
          (download → xz-decompress → raw write, verified by sha256 on the fly),
          then inject the Badger's config. The Badger downloads its own content.
  inject  write config + software into an already-flashed boot partition
  relay   pass-through proxy for a Badger that has no internet of its own;
          bytes stream through memory only — nothing is written to disk
  watch   follow a Badger's provisioning progress
  clone   point a Badger at another Badger on the LAN and pull everything from it

Typical first unit (Badger plugged into your router by Ethernet):
  sudo ./builder/prepper-build flash /dev/disk4 --tier base --ssid HoneyBadger --pin 246813
  ./builder/prepper-build watch badger.local
Extra units copy from the first one over the LAN, using no internet at all:
  sudo ./builder/prepper-build flash /dev/disk4 --tier base --hostname badger2 \\
       --peer http://badger.local/sync --trust-key "$(ssh badger.local cat /etc/prepper/keys/disk_ed25519.pub)"

Standard library only (Python 3.11+). macOS and Linux.
"""
